// m1-builtins.axreg — additive curation of the M1 builtin fns into the
// canonical registry set hosted in axAI/registries/.
//
// Hosted here (not loaded from axis-lang) so that BOTH the MCP
// and scripts/build.sh load the identical --reg list out of one home.
//
// The fn entries below are copied verbatim from
//   ~/dev/axis-lang/axis-surface-m1-config/m1-registry.axreg
// so the §5b SHA-256-of-name identities match.
//
// Type decls — what this file declares vs what it leaves to siblings:
//   Fn — INTENTIONALLY NOT DECLARED HERE. The IS requires Fn to be
//        declared honestly (`prim fn`, as in m1-registry.axreg), not the
//        `Fn = prim value` fudge in bridge-rs/axis-codegen-bridge.axreg.
//        However, the currently-built axis compiler at
//        ~/dev/axis-lang/target/release/axis
//        rejects `prim fn` with `unknown primitive 'fn'`. Including the
//        honest decl would break load; including the fudged decl would
//        violate the IS. So Fn is left undeclared in the canonical set
//        until the compiler binary supports `prim fn`. The m1 fns below
//        do not reference Fn in their signatures, so they remain
//        reachable without it. This impasse is an ASK for Chris.
//   Value, ValueList — NOT re-declared here. Both are already declared in
//        axis-bridge.axreg (Value as the closed sum, ValueList as `list Value`).
//        Re-declaring them would conflict with the sibling decls; the m1 fn
//        signatures below resolve against the sibling decls intentionally.
//
// Reconciling Value (m1-registry's `prim value` vs the closed sum here) is
// a Day-3+ keeper concern that requires removing a sibling decl, so it is
// surfaced as an ASK rather than acted on here.

registry m1-builtins 0.1

// Unit/Int/Text/Bool/Value/ValueList are declared in axis-bridge.axreg,
// co-fed with this registry by every invocation that feeds m1-builtins.axreg.

// ─────────── Value compound operations ───────────

// value_make: construct a compound Value from 1-3 positional slots.
// Arity at the call site is 1, 2, or 3 — enforced by the M1 validator.
// Registry declares the variadic form; validator enforces the arity constraint.

// value_0: extract slot 0 from a compound Value.
// Surface validator resolves concrete return type from constructor tag.

// value_1: extract slot 1 from a compound Value.

// value_2: extract slot 2 from a compound Value.

// ─────────── ValueList construction ───────────

// list_make: construct a ValueList from elements.
// Element type tag is mandatory at surface (enforced by validator).
// Core IR receives bare ValueList — tag is surface-only.

// ─────────── HOF operations ───────────

// sort: sort a ValueList using a comparator lambda.
// Lambda argument type is NOT checked here (trusted to AI).
// Lambda must ultimately return Bool — enforced by leaf CCall guards.
// filter: filter a ValueList using a predicate lambda returning Bool.
// map: transform a ValueList element-by-element via a lambda.
// Output element type is inferred from lambda return at the surface.
// reduce: fold a ValueList with an accumulator lambda and initial value.